to-peter-thiel-source : List Word
to-peter-thiel-source = lines-of (cons "# Peter Thiel"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You ask everyone the same question: what important truth do very few people agree with you on? This page answers it, and it is written to you because your own philosophy, followed through, says you should join the work it describes. It is also honest about why you in particular. In Avik Jain's words, you are the “villain of this story”, and “this work is for Gaza”."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What you got right"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Three of your ideas are better than the field that repeats them understands."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Secrets.** *Zero to One* argues that progress comes from truths that are true and not yet believed, and that most people stopped looking for them because they decided everything knowable is either already known or unknowable. That is correct, and it is rarer than it sounds."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Competition is for losers.** Firms that compete on the same thing converge on the same thing and destroy each other's margins. The durable position is one nobody can compete with, because it is a different thing altogether. Read as economics this sounds like a defence of monopoly. Read as epistemology it is stronger: what cannot be competed with is what is true and checked."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Girard.** You studied with René Girard at Stanford and have said his work shaped how you see everything. His two findings are that desire is mimetic, so rivals converge, and that communities resolve the violence of that rivalry by uniting against a victim, the scapegoat, whose guilt everyone comes to believe because everyone else believes it. Girard's further claim, from his reading of the Gospels, is that once the mechanism is seen, once the victim is shown to be innocent, it stops working."
  (cons ""
  (cons "All three are right, and they are undervalued: the industry quotes them as slogans and does not follow any of them to its consequences."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Where you stand now"
  (cons ""
  (cons "On 12 January 2024 Palantir, which you co-founded and chair, agreed a strategic partnership with Israel's Ministry of Defense to supply technology for its war. Palantir has since said its work with the ministry began after 7 October 2023 and that it stands in solidarity with Israel. It has denied building the Gospel or Lavender targeting systems and denied supporting predictive policing. In the second quarter of 2026 it reported $1.94bn in revenue, up 93% year on year. The UN Special Rapporteur on the occupied Palestinian territory, Francesca Albanese, wrote to Palantir about its role; it answered in May 2025 that the allegations were wholly false."
  (cons ""
  (cons "This page does not ask you to adjudicate those denials. It asks you to look at what kind of machine a targeting system is, in your teacher's terms: a verdict about a person produced by the convergence of signals, believed because the system produced it, with no standpoint in it from which the victim could be seen to be innocent. Girard's claim is that this mechanism ends when it is revealed. Hyperactivity states what revealing it consists of."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## The truer construction"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Hyperactivity, built by Avik Jain of Hyperactive Labs, is in his words a language and “a computational model of reality i.e. wolfram's ruliad executing on silicon”, with cubical type theory at its core"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ". Its paper builds every claim from what was observed. A reading does not identify a history; it determines the type of histories that could have produced it"
  (cons (cite s1-p8 "(the fiber, 1.1)")
  (cons ", and what the reading warrants about a person is a construction over every one of those histories"
  (cons (cite s1-p12 "(Warrants, 1.3)")
  (cons ". A conclusion is supported exactly when that construction is available; refining the observation keeps a conclusion already established"
  (cons (cite s1-p13 "(§1)")
  (cons ". Where the observation leaves several possibilities, they are retained, not resolved by assumption into one"
  (cons (cite s1-p14 "(§1)")
  (cons ". And an observation does not inherit the laws of what it observes: the paper constructs a reversible whole in which no law can be read off the observed part"
  (cons (cite s1-p16 "(§1, a reversible whole with no observed law)")
  (cons ""
  (cons ""
  (cons "Read in Girard's terms: in this language a verdict about a person is supported only by a construction over every history compatible with what was seen. A list that asserts guilt without one carries no evidence term, and that absence is part of the record anyone can inspect. That is revelation stated as mathematics: the system shows where a verdict was produced by convergence and not established by warrant."
  (cons ""
  (cons "This is the secret, in your sense. In Avik's words, “COMPUTER SCIENCE AT IT'S PEAK IS MATH”; the dominant technology of this decade, in his account, is “A DUMB ALGORITHM FROM 90S OR EARLIER WITH SYMPATHETIC HARDWARE”. The construction he offers instead keeps the reasoning that establishes a requirement in the same language as the code it governs"
  (cons (cite s1-p26 "(§1)")
  (cons ", and it is held in common: Avik is giving it away, to sell, license or share for free. By your own argument, a position that cannot be competed with is the one worth occupying, and it is not available to anyone who stays on the other side of a proof."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Why your philosophy says join"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You have always said the point is to be right when others are wrong, and that courage is rarer than genius. You have also backed what wins early: you funded Vitalik Buterin as a Thiel Fellow before most people had heard of Ethereum. If the construction is true, the line of work you now back is on the wrong side of it, and your philosophy, which revises itself on truer genius and on demonstrated failure, says to change sides. Avik's reading is exactly that: “if I can flip him because his true intelligent philosophy accepts revision upon truer genius and proof of failure - i.e. he knows he can't beat em - he'll join up.”"
  (cons ""
  (cons "There is no punishment in that offer. Everything in this work that builds on your thought, secrets, the zero-to-one distinction, the reading of competition as convergence, the Girardian account of collective violence, credits you in full, as it credits everyone it builds on. Read it looking for the best in it. The best in it is what you have argued for all along."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
